# Line endings are content in this repository, not formatting.
#
# Four packages compare something generated to something committed, byte for
# byte: the service definitions (internal/service), the extension contract
# (internal/proxy), the heartbeat golden (pkg/telemetry), and the embedded icons
# (internal/tray). Git on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF at checkout unless told
# otherwise, so all four failed there — and the windows job said only "Test",
# which is why it sat red from the day it was added without anybody knowing what
# it meant.
#
# eol=lf rather than text=auto alone: `auto` still normalises to the platform's
# native ending in the working tree, and the working tree is what `go test` reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched at all. The icons are generated and committed, `go:embed`
# compiles them into the binary, and a byte rewritten in one is an icon that
# does not decode.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
